{"id":"s1.4.5","slug":"remainders-of-expressions","title":"Remainders of Expressions","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">A key principle of modular arithmetic is that \"the algebra of the remainders is equal to the remainder of the algebra.\" Instead of calculating the result of a large expression and then finding the remainder, you can find the remainder of each term first and then perform the algebra on those smaller numbers.</p><p>For $(43 - 15 \\times 43) \\div 6$:<br>1. Find remainders mod 6: $43 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6}$ and $15 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{6}$.<br>2. Perform algebra on remainders: $1 - (3 \\times 1) = -2$.<br>3. Adjust if negative: $-2 \\equiv -2 + 6 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{6}$. The remainder is 4.</p>","summary":"A key principle of modular arithmetic is that \"the algebra of the remainders is equal to the remainder of the algebra.\" Instead of calculating the res","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem asking for the remainder of an algebraic expression (e.g., `(a*b - c) / d`).","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"(31 × 6 − 17) ÷ 8 has a remainder of:","answer":"1","kind":"exact","tags":["remainders"]},{"id":2,"text":"(34 × 27 + 13) ÷ 4 has a remainder of:","answer":"3","kind":"exact","tags":["remainders"]},{"id":3,"text":"(44 × 34 − 24) ÷ 4 has a remainder of:","answer":"0","kind":"exact","tags":["remainders"]},{"id":4,"text":"(33 + 23 × 13) ÷ 3 has a remainder of:","answer":"2","kind":"exact","tags":["remainders"]},{"id":5,"text":"(23 + 33 × 43) ÷ 4 has a remainder of:","answer":"2","kind":"exact","tags":["remainders"]},{"id":6,"text":"(24 × 34 − 44) ÷ 7 has a remainder of:","answer":"2","kind":"exact","tags":["remainders"]},{"id":7,"text":"(11^2 + 9 × 7) ÷ 5 has a remainder of:","answer":"4","kind":"exact","tags":["remainders"]},{"id":8,"text":"(15 × 3 − 6^2) ÷ 9 has a remainder of:","answer":"0","kind":"exact","tags":["remainders"]},{"id":9,"text":"(12 × 9 − 2^3) ÷ 8 has a remainder of:","answer":"0","kind":"exact","tags":["remainders"]},{"id":10,"text":"(65 × 4 − 3^2) 